1
00:00:10,440 --> 00:00:14,000
♪ I've never believed in love ♪

2
00:00:14,000 --> 00:00:17,360
♪ I've never trusted anyone ♪

3
00:00:17,360 --> 00:00:20,040
♪ I've always lived by reason ♪

4
00:00:20,040 --> 00:00:24,360
♪ I've never followed my heart ♪

5
00:00:24,360 --> 00:00:27,640
♪ Locked away with a complicated code ♪

6
00:00:27,640 --> 00:00:32,000
♪ But you broke through
My heavily guarded firewall ♪

7
00:00:32,000 --> 00:00:36,160
♪ That used to protect my heart ♪

8
00:00:37,200 --> 00:00:40,920
♪ I'm in love with you ♪

9
00:00:40,920 --> 00:00:44,640
♪ I've just realized today that love ♪

10
00:00:44,640 --> 00:00:50,680
♪ Is something I should get to know and explore ♪

11
00:00:50,680 --> 00:00:54,040
♪ The code to my heart has been cracked ♪

12
00:00:54,040 --> 00:00:58,040
♪ By the love you wrapped me in ♪

13
00:00:58,040 --> 00:01:00,800
♪ Having you close puts you in my dreams ♪

14
00:01:00,800 --> 00:01:02,240
♪ You're always on my mind ♪

15
00:01:02,240 --> 00:01:04,840
♪ You cracked my code ♪

16
00:01:04,840 --> 00:01:08,040
♪ My heart's security system is disabled ♪

17
00:01:08,040 --> 00:01:11,120
♪ You unlocked my heart with a love ♪

18
00:01:11,120 --> 00:01:16,000
♪ That this world has never given me ♪

19
00:01:16,000 --> 00:01:18,520
♪ Can I write a new code ♪

20
00:01:18,520 --> 00:01:21,360
♪ That says I love you? ♪

21
00:01:21,960 --> 00:01:25,040
♪ Love you ♪

22
00:01:32,720 --> 00:01:34,720
Whenever my heart starts racing,

23
00:01:34,720 --> 00:01:36,880
Kit is always close by.

24
00:01:36,880 --> 00:01:40,120
This is the first time
my heart has raced this hard.

25
00:01:40,120 --> 00:01:42,280
I've diagnosed myself.

26
00:01:42,280 --> 00:01:43,800
I'm in love.

27
00:01:44,760 --> 00:01:46,560
I've finished my master's degree.

28
00:01:46,560 --> 00:01:48,400
Let me apply for a job at your company.

29
00:01:48,400 --> 00:01:50,760
But I want you to get experience elsewhere first.

30
00:01:50,760 --> 00:01:53,000
Kit, I'm grown up now.

31
00:01:53,360 --> 00:01:54,560
I'll prove it to you.

32
00:01:54,560 --> 00:01:56,880
Does he know you're interviewing here?

33
00:01:56,880 --> 00:01:59,600
I want to get the job first, then tell him.

34
00:01:59,600 --> 00:02:01,560
I like people with conviction.

35
00:02:01,560 --> 00:02:03,440
Nice to meet you, Mr. Nontawat.

36
00:02:03,440 --> 00:02:04,560
Likewise.

37
00:02:09,120 --> 00:02:10,080
Shit!

38
00:02:10,080 --> 00:02:11,800
Mr. Roch interviewed you himself?

39
00:02:11,800 --> 00:02:12,840
Yeah.

40
00:02:12,840 --> 00:02:15,080
And he even let me name my own salary.

41
00:02:15,080 --> 00:02:16,280
Holy shit.

42
00:02:16,280 --> 00:02:17,040
That's awesome.

43
00:02:17,720 --> 00:02:21,160
Thanks so much for telling me to apply to RC.

44
00:02:21,160 --> 00:02:22,440
Yeah, no problem.

45
00:02:22,440 --> 00:02:25,240
It'd be great for me if you got a job at RC.

46
00:02:25,240 --> 00:02:27,000
Then I could see you more often.

47
00:02:27,000 --> 00:02:28,760
How's that gonna work?

48
00:02:28,760 --> 00:02:31,280
My office is all the way in Sathorn.

49
00:02:31,600 --> 00:02:33,480
I'm not coming all that way for you.

50
00:02:33,480 --> 00:02:37,560
Don't you know RC is moving into
the same building as my office?

51
00:02:40,520 --> 00:02:41,960
The same building?

52
00:02:44,280 --> 00:02:45,480
Sharp!

53
00:02:45,480 --> 00:02:46,640
- Hey.
- Huh?

54
00:02:46,640 --> 00:02:48,960
What do you mean? The same building?

55
00:02:48,960 --> 00:02:49,760
Yeah.

56
00:02:50,160 --> 00:02:53,080
RC is partnering with NSL, your brother's company.

57
00:02:53,080 --> 00:02:53,680
Partnering?

58
00:02:54,680 --> 00:02:56,080
Why didn't you tell me?

59
00:02:56,080 --> 00:02:57,400
I thought Kit had told you.

60
00:02:57,400 --> 00:02:59,760
I haven't even told him I applied for a job here.

61
00:02:59,760 --> 00:03:01,360
Huh? Why not?

62
00:03:01,360 --> 00:03:03,120
I was gonna surprise him.

63
00:03:03,120 --> 00:03:04,880
You're in for a bigger surprise now.

64
00:03:17,920 --> 00:03:21,560
Kit, I had an interview with RC Capital today.

65
00:03:21,880 --> 00:03:23,880
They gave me a trial assignment.

66
00:03:23,880 --> 00:03:25,760
I'm going to give it my all.

67
00:03:25,760 --> 00:03:27,480
It's a really great opportunity.

68
00:03:32,320 --> 00:03:34,720
If I tell him straight up,
he's gonna get mad.

69
00:03:37,680 --> 00:03:40,400
Kit, today I...

70
00:03:41,120 --> 00:03:42,080
Nope.

71
00:03:42,800 --> 00:03:44,680
Sounds like I'm asking for money.

72
00:03:46,480 --> 00:03:47,280
Okay.

73
00:03:48,800 --> 00:03:50,840
Kit, I have a surprise for you.

74
00:03:52,200 --> 00:03:53,280
What is it?

75
00:03:56,040 --> 00:03:57,080
Uh...

76
00:03:58,760 --> 00:04:00,840
I made you fish steak today.

77
00:04:01,320 --> 00:04:02,760
You do that every day.

78
00:04:03,840 --> 00:04:05,480
But today is different.

79
00:04:06,160 --> 00:04:08,040
Because it's...

80
00:04:08,040 --> 00:04:09,320
trout.

81
00:04:12,240 --> 00:04:13,920
I did some research.

82
00:04:13,920 --> 00:04:16,880
Trout has half the calories of salmon.

83
00:04:17,360 --> 00:04:19,920
So I went to all the big malls looking for it

84
00:04:19,920 --> 00:04:21,080
to make this for you.

85
00:04:22,000 --> 00:04:23,040
It looks great.

86
00:04:23,640 --> 00:04:24,400
I'll dig in.

87
00:04:24,400 --> 00:04:25,560
Go ahead.

88
00:04:26,480 --> 00:04:27,480
Give it a try.

89
00:04:34,600 --> 00:04:36,240
Hmm, it's really good.

90
00:04:37,040 --> 00:04:38,080
Eat up.

91
00:04:57,320 --> 00:04:59,040
Where'd you rush off to this morning?

92
00:04:59,040 --> 00:05:00,640
Is there something I should know?

93
00:05:04,360 --> 00:05:06,360
I was meaning to tell you.

94
00:05:06,360 --> 00:05:08,000
I had a job interview.

95
00:05:08,880 --> 00:05:11,080
So you don't agree with my approach.

96
00:05:11,080 --> 00:05:12,320
That's not it.

97
00:05:12,320 --> 00:05:14,320
I want to try doing things my way.

98
00:05:14,320 --> 00:05:17,400
If it doesn't work out,
I'll pursue a higher degree.

99
00:05:17,400 --> 00:05:18,840
Do you know the result yet?

100
00:05:19,800 --> 00:05:22,080
Not yet. I have to wait for their answer.

101
00:05:26,040 --> 00:05:28,520
It's good that you're looking for a job.

102
00:05:29,120 --> 00:05:30,640
But the real world isn't easy.

103
00:05:31,160 --> 00:05:34,000
If you don't have what it takes, no one will care.

104
00:05:34,480 --> 00:05:36,760
Are you saying I don't have what it takes?

105
00:05:36,760 --> 00:05:37,840
That's not what I said.

106
00:05:37,840 --> 00:05:39,000
Then what are you saying?

107
00:05:40,200 --> 00:05:43,600
Nont, I'm teaching you something.
I don't want you to make a mistake.

108
00:05:45,600 --> 00:05:47,240
Thank you for the lecture.

109
00:05:53,520 --> 00:05:54,320
Sorry.

110
00:05:55,640 --> 00:05:57,840
Yes, Nu. I sent it on LINE.

111
00:06:01,880 --> 00:06:03,960
I just spoke with a university in the US.

112
00:06:03,960 --> 00:06:06,480
I told them my brother
was interested in studying there.

113
00:06:06,480 --> 00:06:07,880
Here's the university info.

114
00:06:19,880 --> 00:06:20,880
Uh...

115
00:06:21,440 --> 00:06:24,400
A master's and a PhD program together?

116
00:06:25,080 --> 00:06:28,640
Yeah. Once you graduate and come back,
you'll have a bright future.

117
00:06:28,640 --> 00:06:30,040
I wanted to repay you

118
00:06:30,040 --> 00:06:32,080
for getting married to me.

119
00:06:32,080 --> 00:06:32,920
Kit,

120
00:06:33,520 --> 00:06:36,160
you don't need to think about repaying me.

121
00:06:37,080 --> 00:06:39,440
I married you because I wanted to.

122
00:06:39,760 --> 00:06:42,040
I want you to think about your own future.

123
00:06:42,960 --> 00:06:43,840
Trust me.

124
00:06:44,240 --> 00:06:46,320
Come back and start your own company.

125
00:06:46,320 --> 00:06:47,680
I'll support you.

126
00:07:39,680 --> 00:07:40,640
Mm.

127
00:07:41,920 --> 00:07:43,080
Let me take a quick look.

128
00:07:45,360 --> 00:07:46,240
Okay.

129
00:07:57,920 --> 00:08:00,760
Kit, do you realize what you're doing?

130
00:08:02,080 --> 00:08:03,160
What am I doing?

131
00:08:04,480 --> 00:08:05,760
Looking at me like that.

132
00:08:08,080 --> 00:08:09,080
Like what?

133
00:08:19,800 --> 00:08:21,600
Don't you feel anything at all?

134
00:08:22,680 --> 00:08:23,760
Feel what?

135
00:08:34,800 --> 00:08:35,880
Never mind.

136
00:08:51,280 --> 00:08:52,880
I should've said it that day.

137
00:08:55,200 --> 00:08:56,800
Then you would've understood.

138
